	(text "Yaesu AC (G-450 class): \nmotor CW  (Yaesu 5) on J1-5, \nmotor CCW (Yaesu 4) on J1-6,\nmotor common (Yaesu 6) and pot ground (Yaesu 3) on J1-1, \npot   REF (Yaesu 1) on J1-3,\npot   wiper (Yaesu 2) on J1-7. \nOpen SJ1/SJ2, close SJ3/SJ4 so the cap sits across the drive ends.\n\nG-5500 and HDR-300 keep the cap in the rotor: \nleave SJ1-SJ4 open and do not fit C1/C2.\n\nHDR-300's pinout is not this 1:1 map. It needs a cable adapter. Cap omitted either way.\nBrake enable AZ_BRAKE_EN high RELEASES the brake. Any fault or ARM drop engages it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 292.354 -25.654 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "34bd69bb-45ff-4318-9599-add6f096fb79")
	)
	(text "CDE terminal block J1, 1:1 with the rotor strip (catalog hygain-ham-iv, V4 sheet note).\n1 ROTOR_RETURN  common: motor, brake, pot wiper\n2 BRAKE         solenoid. Energized = released. Off = wedge engaged\n3 AZ_POT_3      pot end +\n4 CAP / winding end. Run cap across 4 and 8 for CDE (SJ1, SJ2 bridged)\n5 CW            via the right limit switch to terminal 8\n6 CCW           via the left limit switch to terminal 4\n7 AZ_POT_7      pot end -\n8 CAP / winding end\nV4's J3 is a 10-pin Mate-N-Lok. Its pin numbers are not these terminal numbers.\nThe V4 text note (1 Return, 2 Brake, 4 Cap Left, 5 Motor Right, 6 Motor Left, 8 Cap Right)\nmatches this map. Right = CW, Left = CCW."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.732 -14.224 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9fcc164c-5e9a-4229-83f1-f02c5e68c5b4")
	)
